Feature: PetStore API CRUD operations\n\n  Background:\n    Given the API endpoint is \"https://petstore.swagger.io/v2\"\n\n  @create\n  Scenario: Create a new pet\n    When I send a POST request with the following data:\n      | id   | name  | status |\n      | 123  | Doggo | available |\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Doggo\"\n\n  @read\n  Scenario: Get pet by ID\n    When I send a GET request for pet with ID 123\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Doggo\"\n\n  @update\n  Scenario: Update an existing pet\n    When I send a PUT request with the following data:\n      | id   | name  | status |\n      | 123  | Doggo | sold |\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"sold\"\n\n  @delete\n  Scenario: Delete a pet\n    When I send a DELETE request for pet with ID 123\n    Then the response status code should be 200\n    And the response body should contain \"Pet deleted\"\n\n  @negative\n  Scenario: Get non-existent pet\n    When I send a GET request for pet with ID 999\n    Then the response status code should be 404\n    And the response body should contain \"Pet not found\"